Oh, now!

3
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Good morning, Yuki.

4
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Sir, Clydesdale platoon is back from their recon mission to Mazurek Landing Castle.

5
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:17,000
All right, then. Let's open the well, Doc.

6
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:29,000
All units back and glad to be home.

7
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Warrant Officer Kaiska.

8
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Yes?

9
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Clean up and report to the Captain's quarters. You've been requested.

10
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Me?

11
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:43,000
That's right. It's about the Deucalion. It's headed back down here. To the Earth.

12
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Captain, we're told to land at Port Aiden.

13
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Please calculate optimal re-entry time in Vector and report back to me.

14
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Yes, ma'am.

15
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:58,000
We're on the move all the time. They're trying to get as much out of us as they can. Until we're all gone.

16
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:02,000
Are you sure it's not that they just put a high value on what this ship and crew can do?

17
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:07,000
I really don't think they have any idea what to do with us. At least that's the vibe I get.

18
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:11,000
I need your approval, Captain, for the Quartermaster's supply list.

19
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:14,000
I've already checked the list over. Go ahead and send it in.

20
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Yes, ma'am.

21
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Attention, all hands.

22
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:25,000
We're instructed to return to Earth. At 1300 hours UTC, we will begin our re-entry sequence.

23
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Thanks, ma'am.

24
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Thanks, ma'am.

25
00:02:48,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Thanks, ma'am.

26
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:10,000
We'll see you next time.

27
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:17,920
I'm falling, it's not

28
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:19,800
You can do it every single-shot

29
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:22,220
I realize it to be this power

30
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:23,200
based on the success

31
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:25,640
You can do it

32
00:03:25,640 --> 00:03:29,140
My very own world

33
00:03:29,140 --> 00:03:31,840
A sense of action

34
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:34,600
Feel me

35
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:37,860
Charles Teri

36
00:03:37,860 --> 00:03:54,140
Son of a stage.

37
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:02,980
Calvado is quite nice.

38
00:04:02,980 --> 00:04:05,340
Thank you, sir. But no, thank you.

39
00:04:05,340 --> 00:04:06,020
Very well.

40
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:10,560
Tell me, will we really be escorting the Deucalion?

41
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:13,940
Temporarily, while they resupply and refit the ship.

42
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:18,380
Should be uneventful. The base they've been assigned to is close to our position.

43
00:04:19,580 --> 00:04:22,240
The two of you do have some ties to that ship.

44
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:25,160
I understand you chose not to keep serving a boarder.

45
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:30,080
Being a board only opens up old wounds, so I decided not to serve on her.

46
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:32,280
I believe your younger brother is a board.

47
00:04:33,080 --> 00:04:35,840
His exploits have been quite something, I hear.

48
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:37,980
Yes, sir. I guess.

49
00:04:42,320 --> 00:04:43,460
May I, sir?

50
00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:44,420
Certainly.

51
00:05:03,060 --> 00:05:05,720
How did the other nobles react after that?

52
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:12,140
I'm told that none of them are expressing opposition openly. At least in Harklight's opinion.

53
00:05:13,460 --> 00:05:15,640
Do you share that opinion, Slane?

54
00:05:16,740 --> 00:05:21,960
No. They most likely won't be holding back their true feelings very much longer.

55
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:25,620
It would be in bad taste, while we're still mourning the Count.

56
00:05:25,620 --> 00:05:34,300
It is an undeniable fact. Count Sosbom's death is a great loss to verse and to what we want to achieve.

57
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:43,760
I am the result of an indiscretion committed on the moon by my father, the second emperor, Gilzeria.

58
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:51,880
Father perished as a result of his second sin, Heaven's fall. That sin shattered this moon we are on.

59
00:05:51,880 --> 00:06:04,180
Count Sosbom found me and offered his allegiance when I had lost my family, although I never actually knew what he was thinking deep down.

60
00:06:04,180 --> 00:06:11,960
But no matter. When it comes to those who have no talent for scheming, trust becomes more difficult.

61
00:06:11,960 --> 00:06:21,540
Therefore, Slane, you must weather the brunt of their envy and jealousy. Either way, you've inherited all of the Count's privileges,

62
00:06:22,180 --> 00:06:27,140
as well as the special status which accrued to him as the guardian of my sister.

63
00:06:27,700 --> 00:06:32,400
I am prepared for that. A duty which deserves to be envied by all.

64
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:45,880
That noble uniform. You wear it well and it suits you. But there is something you must not forget. The princess that you must protect now is here before you.

65
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:50,380
